<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="MIPS:LE:32:default:default">
<!--
    A MIPS kernel reports a failed system call by setting a3 to 1 (0 on
    success), and the C library tests a3 right after the syscall instruction.
    Unless the call is modelled as writing a3, that test reads the a3 the
    function had on entry, which then becomes a fourth parameter the function
    does not have.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 flow-classification.
    P0 assertion:      option syscallregs off|auto|on  (default auto).

    Source (rd: clang -O2 -target mipsel-linux-gnu -fno-pic -mno-abicalls;
    fail and wr: mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -O2 -fno-pic -mno-abicalls; linked with
    -Ttext=0x100000, the .text bytes verbatim below):

        long rd(long fd, long n) {
          register long a0 asm("$4") = fd + 1; register long a1 asm("$5") = n;
          register long a2 asm("$6") = 16;     register long v0 asm("$2") = 4003;
          register long a3 asm("$7");
          asm volatile("syscall" : "+r"(v0), "=r"(a3) : "r"(a0), "r"(a1), "r"(a2) : "memory");
          return a3 ? -v0 : v0;
        }
        __attribute__((noinline)) long fail(long e) { return -e - 1000; }
        long wr(long fd, long buf) {
          register long a0 asm("$4") = fd + 1; register long a1 asm("$5") = buf + 4;
          register long a2 asm("$6") = 16;     register long v0 asm("$2") = 4004;
          register long a3 asm("$7");
          asm volatile("syscall" : "+r"(v0), "=r"(a3) : "r"(a0), "r"(a1), "r"(a2) : "memory");
          if (a3) return fail(v0) * 3;
          return v0;
        }

    Source at 0x100100 (clang -O2 -target mipsel-linux-gnu -fno-pic
    -mno-abicalls -c, the .text bytes verbatim):

        #define SC(n,x,r,e) do { register long a0 asm("$4") = (x); \
          register long v0 asm("$2") = (n); register long a3 asm("$7"); \
          asm volatile("syscall" : "+r"(v0), "=r"(a3) : "r"(a0) : "memory"); \
          r = v0; e = a3; } while (0)
        long both(long fd) {
          long r1, e1, r2, e2;
          SC(4041, fd, r1, e1); SC(4041, fd + 1, r2, e2);
          if (e1 | e2) return -1;
          return r1 + r2;
        }
        long rd_nocancel(long fd, long buf, long n) {
          register long a0 asm("$4") = fd; register long a1 asm("$5") = buf;
          register long a2 asm("$6") = n;  register long v0 asm("$2") = 4003;
          register long a3 asm("$7");
          asm volatile("syscall" : "+r"(v0), "=r"(a3) : "r"(a0), "r"(a1), "r"(a2) : "memory");
          return a3 ? -v0 : v0;
        }

    rd is the clang form (movz on a3), wr the gcc form (a branch on a3) with a
    call after the syscall while a3 still holds the flag.  Pass 1 (option
    syscallregs on) defines a3 after each syscall with syscall_error(): rd
    and wr take two parameters (rd's n reaches read in place), both test the
    flag, and the flag is not handed to fail as an argument.  Pass 2
    (option syscallregs off) is the vendored model: each function reads the
    entry a3 and grows a fourth parameter.

    both tests two flags, which stay two values: the test is not folded into
    one of them.  rd_nocancel hands its three parameters to read in place;
    the kernel's read takes three registers, so under on the call reads them
    and the function keeps them, without the phantom a3 the vendored model
    adds after them.
-->
